    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full suite is green (64/64 tests pass).\n\n## What I changed\n\n**`identityKey` is now a SHA-256 hex over `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)`:**\n\n- **`mapper/IdentityKey.java`** \u2014 rewrote `of(Owner)` to build the raw string from telephone, lower-cased email, and `soundex(lastName)`, then return the 64-char SHA-256 hex digest (dropping `householdId` from the key).\n- **`mapper/Soundex.java`** (new) \u2014 American Soundex helper delegating to Apache Commons Codec's `Soundex.US_ENGLISH`, returning `\"\"` for a null/blank/unencodable name so it's a safe segment.\n- **`pom.xml`** \u2014 declared `commons-codec` explicitly (it was only transitive) so the Soundex import is a first-class dependency.\n\n**Duplicate detection (409) is now the single identity key:**\n\n- **`CheckOwnerIdentityUnique.java`** \u2014 removed the separate household-duplicate block and the now-unused `sharesHousehold`/`OwnerFieldsDto` parameter. Only an identityKey collision against a non-deleted owner raises `DuplicateIdentityException`. The email-domain blocklist still runs earlier in the pipeline (`CheckEmailDomainAllowed`), unchanged.\n\n**Soft match redesigned:**\n\n- **`CheckPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 now flags `possibleDuplicate` when the identityKey **differs** but `soundex(lastName)` **and** `postcode` both match (dropped the old same-last-name/different-telephone/different-household logic). This is what makes two owners with the same last name + postcode but different telephones a soft match rather than a 409.\n\n**Docs:** updated the stale javadoc in `DuplicateIdentityException` and `AssignHousehold` (which still computes `householdId`, now used only for household sizing in `CountHouseholdMembers`/`CapMembershipLevel`).\n\nThe pre-existing tests that already referenced soundex (`Cp10`, `Cp28`, `Cp35`, `Cp52`) plus all the household/membership tests pass. Note the tests were consistent with this new behavior; no test changes were needed.",
